{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792350653,"nonce":"slTdxMwHqDazwFl9pGJV+bCxS14=","title":"The Ash row trails the Haxe JVM on three of the seven new kernels","message":"Target (user, 2026-10-18): ash should beat the JVM on the kernels added in c3c1b098.\n\nCI sweep on 5c05c82c (median ms, whole process, ubuntu runner; run 39140493728):\n\n    kernel          ash   ash-aot   hxjvm   hashlink-jit\n    fannkuchredux   480     320       795      905\n    spectralnorm    344     233       322     1046\n    pidigits        428     156       877      709\n    fasta           588     393       535      587\n    knucleotide     942     575       462     1331\n    regexredux      125      97       346      189\n    revcomp         121      67       184      420\n\nAhead already: fannkuchredux, pidigits, regexredux, revcomp. Behind in the default Ash (hybrid) row: spectralnorm by 7%, fasta by 10%, knucleotide by 2x; knucleotide also trails with AOT.\n\nWhat the logs show. fasta: randomFasta, which runs 12.5M of its 20M iterations in its second call, never got LLVM code. A loop owner entered once is handed off (no promote), and the check that it is not entered again looked only at interpreter activations; the second call comes from compiled main. A function named by two or more call sites is now promoted. Mac: 514 -\u003e 423 ms. knucleotide: StringMap sized its cells at a quarter of its entries (upstream's choice), so a full table averages four entries per chain, each one a cache miss on a separate hash array; one cell per entry takes the jit row 454 -\u003e 408 ms and hybrid 623 -\u003e 579. spectralnorm: the LLVM code for multiplyAv arrives at 105 ms on the runner and multiplyAtv's compile waits for it on the single promoter thread (142 ms); the 111 ms between hybrid and AOT is Cranelift-speed execution until then.\n\nOpen: remaining knucleotide cost (hbget, boxed Int counts, substr allocation), spectralnorm tier-up latency, and a Linux profile for each (NUC).","files":null}]}